---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Field from '../components/Field.astro';
import { link } from '../lib/links';
---

<Shell
  property="guild"
  dark
  title="Guild — More model. Your machine."
  description="A native, open-source Mixture-of-Experts inference engine. Guild combines GPU VRAM, system RAM, and CPU compute with portable GPACK and hardware-specific GEXEC."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Native inference / open source / v0.x</div><h1>
        More model.<br /><em>Your machine.</em>
      </h1><p class="lead">
        Your GPU is only part of the picture. Guild brings GPU memory, system RAM, and CPU compute
        together to run Mixture-of-Experts models locally.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={link('docs', 'getting-started/')}
          >Build your first run <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/guild-inference/Guild"
          >Explore the source ↗</a
        >
      </div><p class="small-note">C++ · CUDA · HIP / Windows & Linux setup paths</p>
    </div><Field variant="guild" />
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-label">01 / Built for asymmetry</span><div>
        <h2>Not every weight.<br />Not all in VRAM.</h2><p>
          In a sparse MoE model, each token routes through a subset of experts. Guild plans
          execution across the memory and compute available on your machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div><div class="grid-two">
      <div class="paper">
        <div class="eyebrow">Conceptual routing / one layer</div><div
          class="token-controls"
          role="group"
          aria-label="Expert routing example"
        >
          <button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-route="ornith">Ornith · 8 / 256</button
          ><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-route="qwen">Qwen · 10 / 512</button>
        </div><div class="network-grid" aria-hidden="true">
          {Array.from({ length: 256 }, (_, i) => <i class={i % 32 === 7 ? 'on' : ''} />)}
        </div><p id="route-caption" role="status">
          8 of 256 routed experts active per layer. Conceptual selection; not a live model trace.
        </p>
      </div><div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>
            <strong>GPU VRAM</strong><span>Dense path, attention state, cache, scratch</span>
          </li><li>
            <strong>System RAM</strong><span>Routed expert complement & host KV</span>
          </li><li><strong>CPU compute</strong><span>Quantized expert execution</span></li><li>
            <strong>Mapped files</strong><span>Storage-backed expert tier</span>
          </li>
        </ul><p style="margin-top:30px;font-size:14px">
          Designed for large-RAM servers, NUMA systems, and consumer GPUs paired with substantial
          host memory. The runtime finalizes its plan against live free VRAM.
        </p><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:25px" href={link('docs', 'architecture/')}
          >Follow a token through the engine ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-label">02 / Portable model. Local plan.</span><h2>
        The model travels.<br /><em>The tuning stays local.</em>
      </h2>
    </div><div class="flow">
      <span>GGUF<small>Import weights</small></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span
        >GPACK<small>Portable container</small></span
      ><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>GEXEC<small>Machine-specific cache</small></span>
    </div><div class="pillars">
      <article class="pillar">
        <h3>GPACK</h3><p>
          Model weights, architecture metadata, tokenizer assets, and optional expert data in a
          memory-mapped portable container.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('docs', 'gpack/')}>Read the format ↗</a>
      </article><article class="pillar">
        <h3>GEXEC</h3><p>
          Kernel choices, layouts, placement, and calibration bound to model and environment
          identity. A mismatch falls back to portable execution.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('docs', 'gexec/')}>Read the contract ↗</a>
      </article><article class="pillar">
        <h3>Adaptive decoding</h3><p>
          Choose among normal decoding, MTP, lookup, and session-local retrieval. Optimize time per
          committed token, with the target model verifying proposals.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('docs', 'phase66/')}>Read the implementation report ↗</a
        >
      </article>
    </div><p class="small-note">
      Core and these formats remain under development. Calibration combines measured
      microbenchmarks, estimates, and live session observations.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="statement">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">03 / Evidence over headlines</span><h2>
          Performance is<br /><em>a configuration.</em>
        </h2>
      </div><div>
        <p>
          Input-grounded speculative workloads can be much faster. Novel prose, short requests, and
          failed predictions can erase those gains. We publish the workload, hardware, strategy, and
          limitations alongside each selected result.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={link('guild', 'performance/')}>Explore measured results ↗</a
        ><div class="notice">
          <strong>Measured server:</strong> 2× Xeon Gold 6130, 376 GiB system RAM, GTX 1070 8 GiB, Linux.
          RTX 5070 desktop results are pending.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="band">
      <div>
        <h2>Start close to the metal.</h2><p>
          Read the guide. Check compatibility. Build for your hardware.
        </p>
      </div><a class="button" href={link('models')}>Find your model ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-route]');
    buttons.forEach((button) =>
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        buttons.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b === button)));
        const q = button.dataset.route === 'qwen';
        const total = q ? 512 : 256;
        const active = q ? 10 : 8;
        const grid = document.querySelector('.network-grid')!;
        grid.replaceChildren(
          ...Array.from({ length: total }, (_, i) => {
            const node = document.createElement('i');
            if (i < active) node.className = 'on';
            return node;
          }),
        );
        document.querySelector('#route-caption')!.textContent =
          `${active} of ${total} routed experts active per layer. Conceptual selection; not a live model trace.`;
      }),
    );
  </script>
</Shell>
